== Why a state would own its compute

The sovereignty argument is usually made as a legal one — jurisdiction, the CLOUD Act,
where a subpoena can reach. That framing loses, because it is answerable with contract
terms, and hyperscalers have spent five years answering it with contract terms. The
argument that does not dissolve is an operational one: a state that cannot run its own
registry, identity and payment systems through a hostile quarter has outsourced a
function it cannot re-insource on demand.

